; The depth bound on Sarek_ir_interp_value.detach_record (backlog-172 round 4).
; A cyclic [value] is not constructible through the DSL — [@@sarek.type] refuses
; a self-referential field type for lack of a layout — but IS constructible at
; the OCaml level through the mutable [value array] a [VRecord] carries, which
; is what this test does. So the guard is checkable with no device and without
; relying on the unreachability argument holding forever. Own executable because
; it drives sarek.interp directly.

(test
 (name test_detach_record_depth)
 (modules test_detach_record_depth)
 (libraries sarek.interp alcotest))

; backlog-172 round 6. The field-store arm of [assign_lvalue] resolved a field
; name differently from [read_lvalue]: under a REGISTERED type it fell back to
; the positional ([_0]) convention when the helper had no such field, so a name
; the READ refused was WRITTEN into whatever slot sat at that position. Pins that
; write now refuses exactly what read refuses, that the slots are untouched by
; the refusal, and — as the positive controls — that a real field still stores.

(test
 (name test_interp_field_store_resolution)
 (modules test_interp_field_store_resolution)
 (libraries sarek.interp sarek_ir alcotest))

