; backlog-165: the TRIGGER CONDITIONS of Sarek_lower_ir's two ppx-time refusals
; (barrier-bearing constant initializer; a helper that both references and
; rebinds a constant name). Both refusals are `raise_errorf`s and this tree has
; no negative-compile infrastructure, so before this test each was code observed
; firing exactly once by hand. This pins the PREDICATES that decide to refuse,
; not the raise — see the test's header for that boundary stated explicitly.
;
; Links sarek_frontend directly (a plain wrapped-false library with no .mli),
; the same way sarek/tests/e2e/test_stdlib_meta_proof does.

(test
 (name test_lower_ir_refusal_triggers)
 (modules test_lower_ir_refusal_triggers)
 (libraries sarek_frontend))

